= Material Assign =

#type: node
#context: sop
#internal: a3ob_material_assign
#tags: arma, p3d

"""Sets the texture and the material (rvmat) of the polygons in a group, or of all polygons."""

A polygon in a P3D file has a texture and a material (an rvmat file). This node sets them for the polygons in a group, or for all polygons.

@inputs

LOD geometry:
    The LOD whose polygons get the texture and material.

@parameters

Group:
    #id: group

    Which polygons to set. Empty means all polygons. Normal Houdini group syntax; a selection with an encoded name is easiest to pick in the Selection browser.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Group Type:
    #id: grouptype

    Type: Menu. Default: Primitives.

    Primitives:
        The polygons in the group.

    Points:
        The polygons whose points are all in the group.

Set Texture:
    #id: settex

    Off: leave a3ob_texture as it is.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Texture Source:
    #id: texsource

    Where the texture text comes from.

    Type: Menu. Default: File.

    Choices: File, Color, Custom.

Texture File:
    #id: texture

    For File. Slashes are written as backslashes.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Color:
    #id: color

    For Color. Red, green, blue and alpha, 0 to 1.

    Type: 4 numbers. Default: 1, 1, 1, 1.

Color Type:
    #id: colortype

    For Color. The kind of procedural texture.

    Type: Menu. Default: CO - Color Value.

    Choices: CO - Color Value, CA - Texture with Alpha, LCO - Terrain Texture Layer Color, SKY - Sky texture, NO - Normal Map, NS - Normal map specular with Alpha, NOF - Normal map faded, NON - Normal map noise, NOHQ - Normal map High Quality, NOPX - Normal Map with paralax, NOVHQ - two-part DXT5 compression, DT - Detail Texture, CDT - Colored detail texture, MCO - Multiply color, DTSMDI - Detail SMDI map, MC - Macro Texture, AS - Ambient Shadow texture, ADS - Ambient Shadow in Blue, PR - Ambient shadow from directions, SM - Specular Map, SMDI - Specular Map, optimized, MASK - Mask for multimaterial, TI - Thermal imaging map.

Raw Text:
    #id: raw

    For Custom. Copied exactly as typed.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Common Procedural:
    #id: commonproc

    Fill Raw Text from the common procedural textures (and switch Texture Source to Custom). Add your own in the common data file of the Project root and presets tool.

    Type: Menu. Default: none.

    The choices are made when you open the menu, from the geometry or the settings.

Set Material:
    #id: setmat

    Off: leave a3ob_material as it is.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

Material File:
    #id: material

    The rvmat path. Empty clears the material. Slashes are written as backslashes.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Add Common:
    #id: commonmat

    Fill Material File from the common materials (and switch Set Material on). Add your own in the common data file of the Project root and presets tool.

    Type: Menu. Default: none.

    The choices are made when you open the menu, from the geometry or the settings.

The full page for this node is docs/user/reference/a3ob_material_assign.html in the A3OB folder. Open it in a web browser.
